\
This influenza analysis may be run on animal as well as human samples for Research Use Only (RUO). At the current time, the influenza array is not an FDA approved product, nor will it be run in a CLIA (Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments) - certified facility, as CMD is currently awaiting laboratory certification. Those interested in having samples tested will be provided specimen collection kits with appropriate instructions. \
\
"Although our primary focus is on gene-based cancer diagnostics, the flexibility of our technology enables us to rapidly address public health concerns such as viral diseases that have the potential to cause pandemics," stated Matt Watson, CEO of CMD. "We are already in discussions with many domestic and international agencies and we believe this will be a powerful tool for monitoring of the H5N1 Asian Bird Flu." \
\
Dr. Amit Kumar, President and CEO of CombiMatrix Corporation, said, "We are constantly reading reports of birds as well as humans who have been infected with or have died from an influenza. Often these reports indicate that conventional testing was not able to identify the causative influenza strain. Through our molecular diagnostics laboratory, CMD, we wanted to offer our testing services to those who have a need for a very powerful and comprehensive testing service for influenza." \
\
For further information on this service please contact CombiMatrix Molecular Diagnostics at (949) 753-0624 or by email at fluchip@cmdiagnostics.com. \
\
COMBIMATRIX INFLUENZA ARRAY \
\
CombiMatrix's Influenza Microarray is a member of the CombiMatrix CatalogArray(TM) product line and can detect and accurately type flu strains using a protocol that requires less than four hours start to finish. This new microarray can identify H5N1 bird flu as well as provide information on mutations and novel strains of flu not yet seen. The Influenza array provides very-high-resolution genotype information on any given flu strain as well as information on novel strains of flu produced by rapid mutation or recombination between multiple strains of flu. It is designed to work on samples from humans as well as from birds, pigs, horses, dogs, and various other animals. \
\
CombiMatrix CatalogArray's contain in situ synthesized oligonucleotides, prepared using CombiMatrix's patented virtual-flask technology. Sensitivity and performance metrics are available from the company's web site and at www.customarray.com . \
