Current Impact Index: Showcases the broader significance of a company's patents by examining how often its U.S. patents are used as the basis for other innovations in the current year. A value of 100 represents the industry average frequency; therefore a value of 140 would indicate a company's patents have 40 percent more influence on other technologies than an average company in the industry. A value of 80 would indicate a company's patents have 20 percent less influence than an average company. \
