\
Dr. Poste, as R&D chief of SmithKline & French Laboratories in the early 1980s, was among the first in the pharmaceutical industry to embrace the new biotechnology. In the early 1990s, he orchestrated SmithKline Beecham's entry into genomics ahead of his competitors. As director of Arizona State University's Biodesign Institute, he is pioneering a new phase of scientific innovation - the convergence of biology, computing and nanotechnology. Dr. Poste also serves as chair of the U.S. Defense Department's Bioterrorism Task Force. \
