Dr. Caskey, managing director of Cogene Biotech Ventures, served as senior vice president of research for Merck Research Laboratories from 1995 to 2000 and was president of the Merck Genome Research Institute from 1996 to 2000. Previously, as chairman of the Baylor College of Medicine's Department of Human and Molecular Genetics and director of the school's Human Genome Center, he was one of the international leaders in sequencing the human genome. Dr. Caskey is a past president of the International Human Genome Organization. \
