Authentix maintains a Web-based "Track & Trace" program where key product data is stored on a server and updated as it moves through the supply chain. Products are marked with unique license plates which are scanned and attributed to customer shipments. This allows authorized personnel to ensure that genuine product gets to its correct destination and that the source of smuggled product is quickly identified. \
\
M3 (mark, monitor, measure) is a Web-based component of the Authentix anti-counterfeiting plan. Field monitors test products in the supply chain for authenticity and their findings are presented in customized reports to clients. If the need arises, Authentix can provide legal case file support to assist companies with the successful remediation. \
