\
"In order to continue to satisfy technology demands, the HDD industry will need to move to perpendicular recording for smaller form factor, lower price point drives. In response to growth of embedded storage in mobile and wireless applications, our new product line-up delivers both added value and TFMH technology advances, helping our customers meet their increasing areal density and shrinking cost requirements," said Don Kania, Ph.D., Veeco's President and Chief Operating Officer. \
\
To support the needs of the wafer fab, Veeco offers the NEXUS(R) family of products, which allows customers to cluster Veeco's extensive technology portfolio in a common hardware and software architecture. "The data storage industry relies heavily on integrated processing techniques, and the ability to combine multiple deposition and etch steps under continuous vacuum is key to advanced processes for next-generation TFMHs," commented Piero Sferlazzo, Ph.D., Vice President, General Manager of Veeco's Advanced Development Group. "NEXUS provides the most comprehensive and cost-effective process equipment platform in the industry." \
\
In the slider fab, Veeco is introducing a new line of mechanical processing solutions, called the Optium(TM) line of lappers and saws. "Veeco has been able to leverage our extensive knowledge of the slider process flow to develop next-generation lappers and saws. These products are capable of meeting the challenges of perpendicular recording and femto form factor devices, with process control focused on increasing areal density and improving drive reliability," stated Dr. Kania. "Perpendicular recording has placed unprecedented technical demands on the lapping process, which is at the heart of every slider fab. In addition, our customers have directly linked dicing cut-edge quality to drive quality -- better dicing procedures mean less particles and more reliable drives." \
\
Veeco's new product line-up includes: \
\
-- NEXUS Ion Beam Etching systems (NEXUS IBE 420 LE for low-energy sensor and perpendicular pole etch steps) and the NEXUS IBE 420SXi (for improved air bearing etch); \
\
