\
Dr. Drain will be charged with defining and managing NanoGram's long-term technology adoption roadmap. The roadmap includes building upon the company's success in optical nano-composites and applications of nanomaterials in energy products, while also innovating in areas such as self-assembled materials for electronics and composite structures for imaging applications. \
\
"We are delighted to have Kieran join the NanoGram team," said Pete Thomas, Managing Director of ATA Ventures, and NanoGram investor and board member. "Kieran's experience makes him ideal for managing the major growth opportunities NanoGram is addressing in current and future market segments." \
\
Dr. Drain has more than 20 years industrial experience in technology and business management, both in the United States and internationally. Most recently, he served as vice president and general manager of Avery Dennison Corporation's worldwide performance polymers division where he successfully expanded the business in label, graphics and tape applications. Dr. Drain accomplished this by capitalizing on advances in pressure sensitive materials and specialty coatings. \
\
While at Avery, Dr. Drain managed the creation of a start-up business in plastic displays and lithium batteries and directed licensing and joint development programs with OEM partners. Prior to Avery, Dr. Drain served in technical and business leadership roles at Ciba Specialty Chemicals and Loctite Corporation. \
\
"NanoGram will enable new product capabilities in several industries," said Dr. Drain. "The company's intellectual property, process technology and materials expertise uniquely position NanoGram to lead broad adoption of nanotechnology solutions during the next several years." \
