\
The EDA grant will be used to modernize TEN's Sobrato Center for Innovation in San Jose. TEN will soon announce an architecture and engineering team for the planning phase of the project, followed by construction this fall to upgrade the 72,000 sq. ft. facility to support entrepreneurs and start up companies in nanotechnology, biotechnology, and information technology. When fully modernized, TEN's Sobrato Center for Innovation will offer state-of-the-art laboratories and clean rooms, a video conference facility, training rooms, and office space for technology startups and early stage enterprises in Silicon Valley and from around the world. The facility will also become a resource for area university and community college education programs and applied research. \
\
U.S. Secretary of Commerce Carlos M. Gutierrez said, "President Bush and I are committed to partnering with communities to promote innovation and competitiveness. Through economic development grants like these to The Enterprise Network of Silicon Valley, the Commerce Department will continue to encourage investments in local areas, grow the economy and create jobs." \
\
Remarked Congresswoman Zoe Lofgren, "I am pleased that the Department of Commerce is making this vital investment in Silicon Valley's future. Through TEN's stewardship of this $2 million grant, we are taking an important step in supporting the Valley's most important resource -- the entrepreneurs and entrepreneurial spirit that drive innovation and spawns the creation of high growth, high paying jobs." \
\
"The timing is impeccable because it comes on the heels of a recent surge of international interest in Silicon Valley and TEN's incubation model," remarked Dr. Bill Musgrave, TEN's president and CEO. "A fantastic new and modernized TEN Sobrato Center for Innovation will attract U.S. and foreign entrepreneurs, thereby embracing both technological and global economic convergence, while creating jobs and contributing to the Bay Area economy." \
