NEWTON, Mass. - (BUSINESS WIRE) - Aug. 11, 2005 - MFIC Corporation (OTCBB: MFIC) today reported financial results from continuing operations for its fiscal 2005 second quarter and six months ended June 30, 2005. \
\
For the second quarter ended June 30, 2005 the Company reported revenues from continuing operations in the amount of $3,163,645, representing an increase of $81,668, or approximately 3%, from revenues of $3,081,977 for the quarter ended June 30, 2004. Also, for the quarter ended June 30, 2005 the Company posted a net loss from continuing operations of $36,193 or $0.00 per share as compared with net income from continuing operations in the amount of $256,495, or $.02 per diluted share for the quarter ended June 30, 2004. \
\
For the six month period ended June 30, 2005 revenues increased $366,685, or 7%, to $5,700,114, and the Company reported a net loss of $0.02 per share, as compared with $5,333,429, a net profit of $0.02 per diluted share from continuing operations, for the first six months of 2004. \
\
The backlog of orders from continuing operations as of June 30, 2005 were approximately $2.4 million. This compares with a backlog from continuing operations of approximately $2.54 million as of June 30, 2004. \
\
Robert P. Bruno, President & COO commented on the Company's operating performance, "Our sales grew over $627,000, or over 20%, above the first quarter 2005 revenues. Further, year-over-year revenue increased approximately 3%. "Despite our success in increasing sales, profit margins were affected due to pricing concessions granted in recognition of the developmental nature and beta-site status of the first two Constant Pressure equipped systems shipped in the quarter," Mr. Bruno added. "We do not anticipate additional pricing discounts on future orders. The profit margins were also affected by related inventory costs associated with components damaged during production." \
\
Mr. Bruno continued, "Shipments during the quarter were strong and backlog remains relatively robust. We continue to experience solid inquiry, quotation and order activity for all levels of our equipment, a trend which has continued into the third quarter." \
\
Irwin Gruverman, CEO and Chairman stated, "As previously reported in the first quarter of 2004, the Company completed its equity financing and the restructuring of its debt, which allowed it to increase spending on research and development and marketing. On a year-over-year quarterly basis, increased research and development expenditures were $177,345, or an 86% increase and $399,291, or 98% increase for the six month period ended June 30, 2005 over the same period in 2004." \
\
"These costs were driven by continued investments in product development for the Company's core Microfluidizer(R) processor systems and the new patented Microfluidizer Mixer/Reactor (MMR) for production of nanomaterials through fast chemical reactions, as well as an increased focus on our sales and marketing efforts highlighted by our targeted industry market strategy. We intend to continue with this trend for several quarters and anticipate making key hires in strategic areas, where necessary. We also anticipate undertaking a number of developmental projects using our Multiple Stream Mixer/Reactor (MMR) nanoparticle production technology, and other MMR and marketing initiatives." \
\
Mr. Gruverman continued, "With a backlog of over $2.4 million on June 30, 2005 and strong inquiry and order trends, we can reasonably anticipate strong sales performance in the remaining quarters of fiscal 2005. Our objective for the remainder of 2005 and beyond is to balance the reinvestment of our operating cash flow and maintain a modest level of profitability for several quarters." \
\
Second Quarter 2005 Company Highlights \
\
During the quarter, MFIC: \
\
-- Introduced the digitally controlled, Constant Pressure option providing uniform processing pressure in multiple-piston high pressure systems. This feature is expected to lengthen component life and reduce total operating costs, ultimately translating into a competitive advantage and a lower cost of ownership. \
\
-- Shipped two of five orders for Constant Pressure equipped systems received. \
\
-- Increased the Company's expertise and capabilities in the use of instrumentation, automation and monitoring equipment in conjunction with the Microfluidizer processor systems, including both remote control and monitoring through Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (S.C.A.D.A.) and Distributed Control System (D.C.S.) environments. The Company has developed and acquired competence in these areas with our engineering department to enable us to better address our customers' needs. \
\
-- Presented at the NanoEquity Europe 2005 conference in Frankfurt, Germany. The event, sponsored by the Deutsche Boerse, afforded MFIC the opportunity to introduce MMR technology and Microfluidizer processor equipment to European nanotechnology developers, as well as to inform prospective investors of the MFIC advantage in enabling large scale manufacture of nanomaterials. \
\
Notice to Investors/Stockholders \
\
MFIC will hold a conference call at 1:30 PM Eastern Time August 15, 2005 to discuss second quarter financial results. The domestic call in number is 800-683-1525. Management's discussion is expected to be no longer than 20 minutes in duration and will be followed by a question and answer period. For those who cannot listen and participate in the live event, it is anticipated that a replay of the call will be available on the Company's website: www.mficcorp.com . \
\
About MFIC CORPORATION \
\
MFIC Corporation, through its Microfluidics Division, provides patented and proprietary high performance Microfluidizer(R) materials processing equipment to the biotechnology, pharmaceutical, chemical, cosmetics/personal care, and food industries. MFIC applies its 20 years of high pressure processing experience to produce the most uniform and smallest liquid and suspended solid structures available, and has provided manufacturing systems for nanoparticle products for more than 15 years. The Company is a leader in advanced materials processing equipment for laboratory, pilot scale and manufacturing applications, offering innovative technology and comprehensive solutions for nanoparticles and other materials processing and production. More than 3,000 systems are in use and afford significant competitive and economic advantages to MFIC equipment customers. For more information on MFIC and its products, please visit www.microfluidicscorp.com . \
