Expected to surpass $28.5 billion by 2009, the cardiovascular device market segment includes a range of technologies that give doctors options for treating many types of cardiovascular disease including heart failure. Among these technologies are Ventricular Assist Devices, designed to keep sick or injured hearts beating. Other technologies on the market or in development include emergency devices to restart stopped hearts, drug delivery systems, and devices to help physicians assess cardiovascular health and detect and treat potentially life-threatening conditions such as vulnerable plaque. \
