Additionally, those who do not win the auction but elect to join the Mprize Three Hundred - the MPrize's list of givers who commit $1,000 per year for 25 years - will receive an autographed copy of Kurzweil's and Grossman's new book, Fantastic Voyage. \
\
About the MPrize \
\
The Methuselah Mouse Prize ( www.mprize.org ) is the premiere effort of the Methuselah Foundation and is being offered to the scientific research team who develops the longest living Mus musculus, the breed of mouse most commonly used in scientific research. Developing interventions which work in mice are a critical precursor to the development of human anti-aging techniques, for once aging in mice can be effectively delayed or reversed, popular attitudes towards aging as 'inevitable' will be forced to change. When aging in mice is shown to be treatable, the funding necessary for a full-line assault on the aging process will become available. This is the power and hope of the Methuselah Mouse Prize: to demonstrate a proof of principle and show the world that decline in function and age-related disease are no longer inevitable for humanity. \
