\
"As a source of innovation and technology transfer for the global semiconductor industry, we need a metrology tool providing a high accurate measurement data on sub-45nm technologies," said Patrick Dussouillez, Head of Silicon Platform Division, CEA-Leti. "The Yosemite's unique ability to go beyond CD measurements to provide critical feature shape information is essential in that effort. At the 65 nm node and beyond, unmeasured shape variations significantly degrade CD accuracy, but equally important is the critical role the shape itself plays in device performance. The Yosemite is a tool that could provide us with the data we need," said Patrick Dussouillez. \
\
"This JDP with CEA-Leti is truly a win-win for both parties," adds Robert Ricau, Soluris' European vice president of operations. "Using the Yosemite CD-SEM, CEA-Leti will obtain the information needed to develop next-generation technologies, and Soluris will gain insight into the metrology requirements that will be needed at the 65nm, 45nm, and even 32nm process nodes--enabling us to execute solutions to our customer's metrology requirements way ahead of their roadmap." \
