NEWTON, Mass. - (BUSINESS WIRE) - May 12, 2005 - MFIC Corporation (OTCBB: MFIC) today reported consolidated revenues from continuing operations for the quarter ended March 31, 2005 in the amount of $2,536,469, representing an increase of $285,017, or 13% from revenues of $2,251,452 for the same quarter ended March 31, 2004. \
\
For the quarter ended March 31, 2005, the Company posted a net loss from continuing operations of $116,066, or $0.01 per share, after a tax benefit in the amount of $77,000, as compared with net loss from continuing operations of $55,183, or $.01 per share for the quarter ended March 31, 2004. \
\
Operating expenses from continuing operations increased to 1,573,188 for the quarter ended March 31, 2005 from $1,277,729 for the quarter ended March 31, 2004, an increase of $295,459, or 23%. The year-over-year rise in operating expenses related largely to an increase in R&D expenses driven by continued investments in product development for the Company's core Microfluidizer(R) processor systems and the new patented Microfluidizer Mixer/Reactor (MMR) for production of nanomaterials through fast chemical reactions, as well as an increased focus on our sales and marketing efforts highlighted by our targeted industry market strategy. \
\
These results reflect the ongoing operations of the Company's sole operating subsidiary, Microfluidics Corporation, and exclude the discontinued operations of the divested Morehouse-COWLES Division. \
\
The Company reported order backlog at March 31, 2005 of approximately $2,925,000, up more than 60% from $1,830,000 as of March 31, 2004. \
\
"We continue to see strong order, inquiry and quotation levels for laboratory, pilot production and high volume production equipment," said Robert P. Bruno, President & COO. "First quarter 2005 sales were, as indicated earlier this year, lower than the strong sales in the quarter ending December 31, 2004, by about $1,360,000, due to receipt of several orders too late in the quarter to permit manufacture and shipment. However, we experienced year-over-year growth and demonstrated strength driven primarily by sales of the M-700 Series production equipment," added Mr. Bruno. \
\
MFIC also notes that fluctuations in quarterly revenue are common for capital equipment manufacturers and that year-to-year analysis is a more valid tool for assessing sales, growth and stability. \
\
"We remain confident in the ongoing and increased demand for our advanced materials processing equipment across our targeted industry markets, particularly in the biopharmaceutical market," said Irwin Gruverman, CEO and Chairman. "Based on our backlog, order, quotation and inquiry levels, the strong interest in the M-700 series and continuing interest in our laboratory units, we remain committed to reaching a sales target in excess of 2004 revenue of $12.2 million. \
\
First Quarter 2005 Company Highlights \
\
During the quarter, MFIC: \
\
-- Introduced to customers a process that enables spatial arrangement of carbon nanotubes used in specific manufacturing applications. This process has been successfully tested by Carbon Nanotechnologies, Inc., a Texas-based leading manufacturer of single wall and small diameter carbon nanotubes. \
\
-- Increased and diversified marketing efforts to key targeted industries with advertising and direct mail campaigns and the hiring of Gray & Rice Public Relations, Inc. \
\
-- Increased awareness in the investment community with the issuance of a research report and updates written by Taglich Brothers, Inc. and the recent hiring of LaVoie Strategic Communications Group, Inc. for investor relations counsel and financial communications. \
\
First Quarter Stock Trading Activity \
\
-- Husic Capital Management ("Husic") has made a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission indicating that it had recently sold 327,530 shares of MFIC. Previously, Husic's most recently filed reports indicated that it held a 16.2% ownership position in MFIC. The recent sales indicate that Husic's percentage ownership of the Company has been reduced to approximately 12.8%. \
\
Notice to Investors/Stockholders \
\
MFIC will hold a conference call at 1:30 PM Eastern Time May 16, 2005 to discuss first quarter financial results. The domestic call in number is 800-683-1525. Management's discussion is expected to be no longer than 20 minutes in duration and will be followed by a question and answer period. For those who cannot listen and participate in the live event, it is anticipated that a replay of the call will be available on the Company's website: www.mficcorp.com . \
\
MFIC CORPORATION \
\
MFIC Corporation, through its Microfluidics Division, provides patented and proprietary high performance Microfluidizer(R) materials processing equipment to the biotechnology, pharmaceutical, chemical, cosmetics/personal care, and food industries. MFIC applies its 20 years of high pressure processing experience to produce the most uniform and smallest liquid and suspended solid structures available, and has provided manufacturing systems for nanoparticle products for more than 15 years. \
\
The Company is a leader in advanced materials processing equipment for laboratory, pilot scale and manufacturing applications, offering innovative technology and comprehensive solutions for nanoparticles and other materials processing and production. More than 3,000 systems are in use and afford significant competitive and economic advantages to MFIC equipment customers. \
