\
"When we formed Kopin with wafer engineering technologies developed at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, we did not realize how challenging it was to apply our disruptive technologies to generate products that people really need," said Dr. John C. C. Fan, president and CEO of Kopin. "I am proud that we now have products in such wide use today that are changing the way people see, hear and communicate." \
\
Vision 2005, an event taking place on April 25, 2005 at Kopin's Westborough, Mass. facility, will showcase futuristic, theater-quality video in an array of mobile devices containing Kopin's microdisplays. Invited dignitaries, customers, partners, media and analysts will experience, with their own hands and eyes, devices such as personal video eyewear, high-end cameras, camcorders, pocket-sized phone accessories, thermal weapon sights, and more. Guests will sample solutions from established technology giants like Samsung, JVC, Konica Minolta, Nokia, Philips and BAE Systems, as well as emerging video eyewear suppliers such as Icuiti, MicroOptical, Accupix and Oriscape. Guests will also tour Kopin's state-of-the-art manufacturing facility. \
