\
The GEP, a division of the U.K. Trade & Investment office, champions new business ideas by bringing together entrepreneurs and those who can best guide them towards success in the U.K. A unique and valuable aspect of the program is the "Dealmaker" model for mentoring life science- and technology-oriented start-ups. The Dealmakers are experienced, serial entrepreneurs who assist U.S. entrepreneurs by connecting them to a range of resources in the U.K. - notably, introductions to business, technology and financial networks. Often, the Dealmakers find entrepreneurs that are underserved by the U.S. venture capital market - and in so doing fill an important niche in the market. \
\
Wilson Waterworth joins three other Dealmakers previously appointed by the GEP. The existing Dealmakers have VC and entrepreneurial experience in both the U.S. and the U.K. in the technology sector. The GEP is already working with 85 entrepreneurs, 15 of which have successfully developed businesses or opportunities in the U.K. GEP clients include entrepreneurs in the areas of nanotechnology, information & communication technology, pharmaceutical development and diagnostic testing. \
\
Mark Donougher, Head of Entrepreneurial Inward Investment, GEP, for the UKTI noted, "The U.K. is a very entrepreneur-friendly culture and our Dealmakers can help U.S. entrepreneurs more easily access the resources they need. The Programme has already had tremendous success helping entrepreneurs convert IP into businesses with financing, experienced management, and relationships with peers in the U.K. Toby will help us continue to expand our portfolio of clients in the areas of biotechnology, bioinformatics and pharmaceutical development." \
