CEO Michael Weiner Outlines Investment Strategies for the Biomedical Marketplace, Presentation to be Webcast to Public \
\
Biophan Technologies, Inc. (OTCBB: BIPH), a developer of next-generation biomedical technology, has announced that it will be a presenting company at the Sachs-Bloomberg North America Forum for Investing & Partnering in Biotech & Medtech, a leading investment industry conference focused on advanced biotechnology business and investing, to be held at the Fairmont Copley Plaza Hotel in Boston, MA, March 16-17. \
\
Biophan CEO Michael Weiner is scheduled to speak today at 10:55 a.m. The audio portion of his presentation will be simultaneously webcast. To listen to the webcast, visit http://www.vcall.com/CEPage.asp?ID=91005 before the scheduled start of the presentation. \
\
Mr. Weiner will discuss Biophan's advanced nanotechnology and other solutions for products and product enhancements for important medical technology sectors, including Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI). Mr. Weiner will discuss some of the latest science and business involving cutting-edge solutions for safety and compatibility of implanted medical devices and surgical instruments in the MRI environment. He will also provide a perspective on investment conditions within important emerging biotechnology markets. \
\
The forum is organized under partnership of Sachs Associates and Bloomberg Associates. Themes of discussion during the current two-day forum are to include: Venture Financing and Biotech Investing, Bio-Partnering and Collaborations, and MedTech Industry Analysis. For more information about the Forum, please visit www.sachsforum.com/boston05_fs.html . \
\
About Sachs Associates \
\
Sachs Associates is a London-based company which organizes and produces securities markets conferences in association with Bloomberg L.P. Sachs Associates' investment conferences focus on Emerging Markets, European Equities, and Technology, and are held in major financial centers around the world, including London, New York, Zurich, and others. \
\
