The collaboration between Advance Nanotech and Dr. Stevens of Imperial College London will develop composites incorporating nanoparticles for drug delivery applications, a project inspired by the intelligence of biological systems in sensing changes in their environment. These nanoparticle composites will be capable of drug delivery in previously inaccessible parts of the human body by detecting physiological changes in the human body triggering the release of stored drugs. A drug delivery device created using this research could be more sensitive and offer more control over a multitude of different drug dosages. \
