PERTH, Australia - (BUSINESS WIRE) - March 11, 2005 - pSivida Limited (NASDAQ:PSDV; ASX:PSD; Xetra:PSI) today updated shareholders through the submission of a Shareholder Update with the Australian Stock Exchange. The update, which highlights key accomplishments made by the company during the past six months is available at the company's website: http://www.psivida.com . \
\
In the update, the company reports on key milestones achieved. These include: \
\
-- NASDAQ listing in connection with the company's intention to increase its presence and capabilities in the US, including the intention to seek the appointment of a US based CEO and Business Development executive to assist in accelerating the commercialization efforts for BioSilicon(TM). \
\
-- Increasing the awareness of pSivida in the US through presentations at well-known conferences, meetings and in investor newsletters and industry publications. \
\
-- Excellent progress with the development of the company's lead product, BrachySil(TM) for the treatment of inoperable primary liver cancer by effective delivering radiation directly to the tumor. Further interim data recently released form the current Phase IIa clinical trial showed that BrachySil(TM) led to significant regression of tumors. The results revealed an average reduction in tumor size of 80 percent with some small tumors disappearing completely. The company believes that BrachySil(TM) can be registered as an approved treatment for liver cancer potentially as early as 2007. \
\
-- The intended expansion of the use of BrachySil(TM) for other solid tumor cancers, which is expected to ultimately produce a pipeline of BioSilicon(TM) based oncology products. This strategy is expected to broaden the market potential of the product well beyond the possibilities for current brachytherapy and embolisation approaches. In connection with this, the company plans to commence a human clinical trial for a second cancer indication, such as pancreatic cancer, within the next year. \
\
-- The company is currently seeking and is in discussions with development and marketing partners in an effort to maximize the future return to shareholders for BrachySil(TM). \
\
-- The signing of a deal with a top five global pharmaceutical company to evaluate pSivida's BioSilicon(TM) technology for drug delivery. \
\
-- The signing of an agreement with ITOCHU Corporation of Japan, to develop and commercialize BioSilicon(TM) products in Japan and Asia. This Agreement is an important one as ITOCHU is one of Japan's largest companies and the agreement covers opportunities for production, distribution, direct investment, licensing and cooperative development programs as well as the development of entirely new applications for BioSilicon(TM) \
\
-- The creation of Australian-based subsidiary, AION Diagnostics Limited, for a planned future spin-off. This division will develop diagnostic applications for BioSilicon(TM). Dr. Anna Kluczewska has been appointed Managing Director of AION. \
\
-- The appointment of Dr. Mark Parry-Billings as new Research & Development Director. Dr. Parry-Billings is a former Director of R & D at Innovata Biomed and has held senior roles as Schering Healthcare (UK). \
\
-- The growth of the company's UK operations, which now consists of a current staff of 22, of which some 15 hold Ph.Ds. \
\
-- The strengthening of the company's patent positions with a new European patent granted for "Biomirrors", a novel form of BioSilicon(TM) that can be used in the blocking of light as a means to protect the skin from harmful UV rays. In addition, a European patent was granted for the oral delivery of BioSilicon(TM) and, in the US, a patent was granted for silicon fabricated products which overcome the problems normally associated with the damage to circuits caused by high temperature welding. \
\
About pSivida Limited \
\
pSivida is a global nanotechnology company committed to the biomedical sector and the development of products in healthcare. The company's focus is the development and commercialization of a modified form of silicon (porosified or nano-structured silicon) known as BioSilicon(TM). As a new and exciting biocompatible material, BioSilicon(TM) offers multiple potential applications across the high growth healthcare sector, including controlled release drug delivery, targeted cancer therapies (including brachytherapy and localized chemotherapy), tissue engineering and orthopedics. Potential diagnostics applications are being developed through its subsidiary AION Diagnostics Limited. More information is available at www.psivida.com . \
