\
Applied NanoWorks Announces Optically Transparent Pinnacle Zinc Oxide \
444 words\
24 February 2005\
14:45 GMT\
Business Wire\
English\
(c) 2005 Business Wire. All Rights Reserved.\
WATERVLIET, N.Y. - (BUSINESS WIRE) - Feb. 24, 2005 - \
\
New Zinc Oxide Suspension Delivers the First Optically Clear Coating and Additive for UV and Anti-Bacterial Applications \
\
Applied NanoWorks, Inc. today announced the immediate availability of its improved Pinnacle Zinc Oxide, a water based colloid that delivers optical transparency, neutral pH and particle sizes below 10nm in a suspension that utilizes no coatings or surfactants. \
\
Zinc Oxide is best known for its ultra-violet light absorbing capabilities as well as its antibacterial effects. Application areas include electronics, cosmetics, coatings and other personal care products. Historically, even the smallest zinc oxide particles have delivered suspensions that were cloudy. Pinnacle Zinc Oxide is the first 100% transparent zinc oxide suspension available in the zinc oxide market. \
\
"Pinnacle Zinc Oxide establishes a new benchmark for markets and products requiring UV absorption and optical clarity. Interest in transparent suspensions that improve product performance has been very high and our crystalline zinc oxide is the first material to deliver on these requirements," said Eric Burnett, president percent CEO of Applied NanoWorks. "Our next priority is on increasing our manufacturing capacity to keep up with demand." \
\
According to Freedonia Group, nanoscale zinc oxide was a $4MM market in 2000 and will show a CAGR of 56% through 2007 to $90MM. From 2000 to 2020 a continued manufacturing shift from traditional metal oxides to nanoscale metal oxides will occur with nanoscale zinc oxide demonstrating an overall growth rate of 24% to an estimated $350MM by the year 2020. \
\
Pinnacle Zinc Oxide's particles have a median size below 5nm with tight size distributions which enables its unique suspension. No coatings are applied to the zinc oxide nor are any surfactants used to aid in suspending the particles. Neutral pH and 10% solids content combine with particle purity to increase the suspension's flexibility and performance in manufacturing and gives product engineers and researchers maximum functionality. \
\
"Our ability to produce transparent UV absorption through our new zinc oxide suspension will enable a whole new generation of technically superior products and improve performance in many industries," CTO Partha Dutta, Ph.D., stated. "Our suite of production capabilities allows us to achieve material performance only dreamed of until now." \
\
Applied NanoWorks provides high quality nanomaterials services to meet both industrial research and manufacturing needs. Its proprietary technology offers high quality semiconductor, metal and oxide nanomaterials ranging from 2nm to 100nm and are available in volumes ranging from research quantities to high volume purchasing and production agreements. Visit the company's web site at http://www.appliednanoworks.com . \
\
Applied NanoWorks Eric Burnett, 518/276-3246 www.appliednanoworks.com\
