In November 2004, the Wall Street Journal listed clothing with wrinkle-free and anti stain properties as one of the top apparel trends for 2005. The market for wrinkle-resistant clothing continues to grow; 46 percent of men's cotton slacks in the United States offer wrinkle-resistant features. (Source: Textile Consumer Newsletter -- Cotton, Inc.) \
