\
Nextreme is developing next generation thin-film superlattice thermoelectric devices for applications that require extreme thermal management. Thermoelectric devices are heat pumps that can move heat from one point to another, or generate power from a thermal gradient. They can provide cooling, heating, precise temperature control, and convert heat into electricity. Nextreme's superlattice material, when placed directly under a hot spot, can efficiently pump heat out of the semiconductor package. The form-factor of this ultra-thin thermoelectric device enables direct integration onto the semiconductor silicon or into the chip package, providing a solid-state solution with no moving parts. \
