NEW YORK - (BUSINESS WIRE) - Jan. 27, 2005 - Citigroup Depositary Receipt Services, the leading depositary bank, announced today that it has established an American Depositary Receipt (ADR) Program for pSivida Limited, a global nanotechnology company committed to the biomedical sector and developing products in health care. pSivida is headquartered in Perth, Australia. \
\
The ADRs are now listed on the Nasdaq under the symbol PSDV (CUSIP 74439M 10 7). Each Nasdaq traded ADS represents 10 ordinary shares trading on the Australian Stock Exchange (ASX:PSD). pSivida is also listed on the Frankfurt Stock Exchange (PSI). \
\
"We look forward to supporting pSivida as the company expands its presence in the U.S. market and builds investor interest," said Sanjeev Nanavati, Managing Director of Citigroup Depositary Receipt Services. \
\
"The Nasdaq listed ADR program will be an important step forward for pSivida as it looks to achieve success in the U.S., which is both the world's largest capital market and the greatest market for pharmaceutical products," said Gavin Rezos, pSivida Managing Director. "We are actively looking to expand our investor base in the U.S. and are very pleased to appoint Citigroup as our depositary bank." \
\
pSivida Limited is a global biotechnology company committed to the improvement of healthcare through nanotechnology. Its focus is the development and commercialization of a new biomaterial, nano-structured porous silicon (BioSilicon(TM)), for multiple potential applications in healthcare with a core focus on drug delivery. Near term applications of BioSilicon(TM) include slow release drug delivery, targeted cancer therapies (brachytherapy), conventional vaccine and DNA vaccine delivery, orthopedics, tissue engineering and diagnostics. The company's commercialization strategy involves a combination of internal product development, licensing of the BioSilicon(TM) technology platform, and the potential sale of non-core intellectual property. For further information visit www.pSivida.com \
\
